# Raw API caches and generated metadata/tags/embeddings are regenerable
# from scripts, but ARE tracked for the CI sync workflow (see
# .github/workflows/sync-books.yml): each run only fetches/tags/embeds
# books not already present in these files, so they must persist across
# runs. GitHub Actions runners are ephemeral with no other shared disk, so
# "regenerable" here means "committed" -- untracking these would force a
# full (paid) re-fetch/re-tag/re-embed of every book on every sync. CI
# keeps all four provider/text-variant combinations in sync (local is
# free API-wise and openai is a fraction of a cent per book either way).

# Local Netlify folder
.netlify
